From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] web: "Expand clock" in the timing widget, as in Qt
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Qt GUI's timing widget has an "Expand clock" setting, off by
default: a path's clock network, every clock node after the source up
to the register's clock pin, is one "clock network delay" row, its time
the arrival at the clock pin and its delay the network's insertion. On a
design with a deep clock tree the clock rows outnumber the data path's.
The web viewer always listed every clock pin.

An "Expand clock" checkbox on the timing toolbar does the same here, off
by default, for the data and the capture path. A click on the summary
row highlights the register's clock pin.

Upstream: The-OpenROAD-Project/OpenROAD#11859 (draft).

---
